<tr><td style=3D"padding:0 32px 8px;"><h1 style=3D"font-family:Georgia,serif;=
font-size:28px;">The bond market is starting to say the quiet part</h1></td><=
/tr>
<tr><td style=3D"padding:0 32px 16px;"><p style=3D"color:#777;font-size:14px;=
">By <a href=3D"https://example.com/authors/amy-field">Amy Field</a> &#183; 6=
 minute read</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style=3D"padding:0 32px 16px;"><img src=3D"https://cdn.example.com/bo=
nds-hero.jpg" width=3D"536" alt=3D"A trading floor screen showing bond yields=
" /></td></tr>
<tr><td style=3D"padding:0 32px 12px;"><p style=3D"font-family:Georgia,serif;=
font-size:16px;line-height:24px;">Markets spent most of Tuesday pretending th=
at nothing had happened, which in this cycle is its own kind of news. The ind=
ex closed up eleven points, a move so small it barely qualifies as an opinion=
, and yet the underlying plumbing told a much less calm story.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style=3D"padding:0 32px 12px;"><p style=3D"font-family:Georgia,serif;=
font-size:16px;line-height:24px;">Underlying yields rose for the fourth strai=
ght session. That matters because everything in the last two years has been p=
riced off the assumption that borrowing costs had peaked. Four straight up da=
ys in the long bond is the market starting to doubt that assumption out loud.=
</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style=3D"padding:0 32px 12px;"><p style=3D"font-family:Georgia,serif;=
font-size:16px;line-height:24px;">The energy complex was the other tell. Crud=
e sold off hard into the London close, then quietly recovered in the American=
 afternoon. Nobody at the exchanges will say why, and the volume profile sugg=
ests a single large seller rather than a change in fundamentals.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td class=3D"promo" style=3D"padding:16px 32px;background:#fffbea;"><p st=
yle=3D"font-size:13px;color:#666;"><strong>SPONSORED</strong> Our friends at =
Ledger Wealth will rebalance your portfolio for a flat fee. <a href=3D"https:=
//ads.example.com/click?id=3D99">Learn more</a> and get 20% off your first ye=
ar.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style=3D"padding:0 32px 12px;"><p style=3D"font-family:Georgia,serif;=
font-size:16px;line-height:24px;">=E2=80=9CWhat we are hearing from clients i=
s not fear, it is fatigue,=E2=80=9D said one rate strategist at a large deale=
r bank, speaking on condition of anonymity because he is not authorized to ta=
lk to press. =E2=80=9CEveryone wants the all-clear signal, and nobody wants t=
o be the one who says it too early.=E2=80=9D</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style=3D"padding:0 32px 12px;"><p style=3D"font-family:Georgia,serif;=
font-size:16px;line-height:24px;">Equity breadth, meanwhile, was ugly. Roughl=
y a third of constituents closed lower even as the headline index rose, which=
 is what a narrowing market looks like before it stops being a narrowing mark=
et.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style=3D"padding:0 32px 12px;"><p style=3D"font-family:Georgia,serif;=
font-size:16px;line-height:24px;">For the retail investor, none of this is ac=
tionable on its own. It is, however, a reminder that a portfolio built for a =
world of falling rates is a portfolio with one assumption holding it up, and =
assumptions are cheaper to test than to repair.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style=3D"padding:0 32px 12px;"><p style=3D"font-family:Georgia,serif;=
font-size:16px;line-height:24px;">Tomorrow brings the inflation print, and wi=
th it the first chance in six weeks for the bond market to be either vindicat=
ed or wrong in a way that everyone can agree on. Until then, eleven points.</=
p></td></tr>
